WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
- Alright, so I always
enjoy ending the show

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.670
with something fun, or something I love.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.210
And today I am bringing you both.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.523
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.180
So back in March, I
paired up with Snoop Dogg

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.590
to bring a version of
Eurovision Song Contest

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.240
here to the US, it was an amazing show.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.160
And for the past few months,
we've seen incredible artists

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.510
from all 50 states, five US
territories and Washington, D.C.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:28.250
and it was just really cool
to see everybody representing

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.700
all these different territories or states

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.360
that you maybe didn't know a lot about

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.600
musically or culturally.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.140
And the songs were incredible.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.140
And I've loved seeing so much diversity

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.740
in the genres and all these artists.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.152
And a couple days ago,
a jury of their peers

00:00:40.152 --> 00:00:43.160
and you, America, crowned a winner.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.520
She seemed unstoppable from the start

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.200
with her song, "Wonderland".

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.210
Here is Oklahoma's K-Pop queen, Alexa,

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.310
in her winning moment.

00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:54.003
- [Announcer] That means Oklahoma

00:00:54.003 --> 00:00:58.612
is the first ever winner
of American Song Contest.

00:00:58.612 --> 00:01:01.779
Congratulations to Alexa and Oklahoma!

00:01:04.323 --> 00:01:06.515
(audience cheering)

00:01:06.515 --> 00:01:08.999
- [Kelly] Come on over here
Alexa, come get your award!

00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:11.999
(audience cheering)

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.740
- Oh man, I was, like, so busy
hosting, I missed the moment,

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.830
and thanks to that win you will see her

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.800
at the Billboard Music Awards Sunday,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.350
but we have her here now.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.436
Everybody say hi to Alexa.

00:01:29.436 --> 00:01:31.330
(audience cheering)

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.520
So is that, were you just like so floored?

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.353
Did you think -

00:01:34.353 --> 00:01:35.570
'cause there were so many
talented people there,

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.520
and it was like apples and oranges, like,

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.353
comparing all these artists.

00:01:38.353 --> 00:01:39.200
- Exactly. Exactly. I mean,

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.677
even from when just the first
qualifier episode started,

00:01:41.677 --> 00:01:44.290
everybody had their own
little, like, flavor,

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.650
their own little spice to them.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.140
It was kind of hard to choose,
you know, who could win.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.970
Everybody could, it was
anybody's game honestly.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.210
But with that whole result
being announced last night,

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:55.370
it was just so emotional 'cause
my mom, my dad was there.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:57.450
My team all the way from
Korea was there as well.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.390
We had someone from Germany
fly in from our team.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.861
It was just very emotional.

00:02:01.861 --> 00:02:02.830
- I love it.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.835
And I know I told you this
the other day on the carpet

00:02:05.835 --> 00:02:07.561
when we were after the show,

00:02:07.561 --> 00:02:09.030
talking to all the photographers

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.800
and the news outlets and everything,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.570
but it was funny 'cause
the very first text

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.060
I got about this show was from Shelton,

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.370
that I work with on "The Voice".

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:20.170
And he was like, there's a girl
singing K-Pop from Oklahoma?

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.390
And he was like, he was like, wait, what?

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:25.320
And that's what I loved about
it. I thought it was so cool.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.433
Especially you winning, 'cause
I think we think we know

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:30.480
what every state is like,
and every person in it,

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.410
and what they listen to,
and like, we do that.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.970
We diminish people's like, you know,

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.640
versatility and love of
music or the arts in general,

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.473
or anything.

00:02:40.473 --> 00:02:43.450
And I thought it was so cool
that you came from Oklahoma

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.960
and then you ended up just
dominating this competition.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.920
The performance is incredible.
Your voice is incredible.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.260
The dancing was super cool.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.481
Anyway, thank you for being
just such a positive influence

00:02:51.481 --> 00:02:53.810
for everybody out there,

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.900
but also just such a fiery performer

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.440
that really inspires other performers.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.630
That's what I thought was so cool.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.830
All you artists were so
supportive of each other.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:01.847
- Thank you.

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:02.730
- [Kelly] It wasn't like you were fighting

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:03.655
to see who was better.

00:03:03.655 --> 00:03:04.538
- We were so close.

00:03:04.538 --> 00:03:05.860
- You were really like
dancing and singing.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.130
Everybody was cheering everybody on,

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.431
it was a really cool vibe, yeah.

00:03:08.431 --> 00:03:09.264
- [Alexa] Thank you so much, Kelly.

00:03:09.264 --> 00:03:10.690
- Yeah. Congratulations.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.523
- [Alexa] Thank you.

00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:12.356
- [Kelly] Get sleep.

00:03:12.356 --> 00:03:13.867
- I will tonight, thank you.

00:03:13.867 --> 00:03:14.950
- Well, thank you Alexa.

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.703
I'm liking those posts right now.

00:03:20.025 --> 00:03:22.200
So, usually at this point in the show,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.470
we give our guests $1000 courtesy
of our season-long partner

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.770
Pilot Pen, makers of Frixion,

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:28.400
the go-to erasable pen at
"The Kelly Clarkson Show".

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.350
But she got a great life right now.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.040
I figured maybe today it's gonna
be someone in the audience.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.910
So maybe you wanna look under your chair.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:38.530
Maybe you're the one with
$1000, I'm just saying.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.600
Who's got it? Who's got it?

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.854
No one had it?

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:46.854
(Elon screaming)
(audience cheering)

00:03:49.852 --> 00:03:51.422
- Yes! Okay!

00:03:51.422 --> 00:03:55.832
- (laughing) Oh my God. Oh my God.

00:03:55.832 --> 00:03:59.600
I was like, oh my God, what's
your name, where are you from?

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.160
- Hi, my name is Elon. I just
relocated here from Miami.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:03.993
- Oh, awesome!

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.430
Well have so much fun

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.419
and go on a little
shopping spree, all right?

00:04:08.419 --> 00:04:09.252
- Thank you.

00:04:09.252 --> 00:04:11.140
- Just, you know, be careful. Liability.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.790
Don't hit anyone with that chair.

